This repository is the open-source orchestration layer extracted from the
Recoder monorepo (recoder.xyz), a Cursor-like coding agent product. All
packages here are MIT-licensed and were already decoupled, runtime-agnostic
contract/SDK packages inside that monorepo before extraction.

Attribution for portions derived from or designed to interoperate with
third-party sources:

================================================================================
herdr — https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr (vendored by Recoder as "Loom")
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

`packages/agent-runtimes/src/adapters/loom/*` is a clean-room TypeScript
client implementing herdr/Loom's documented Unix-socket terminal-manager wire
protocol (protocol-20). It does not vendor or copy herdr's Rust source; it
implements a compatible client against the protocol described in herdr's
`src/api/schema/*.rs`. No herdr source code is included in this repository.

================================================================================
beads — https://github.com/steveyegge/beads
`packages/beads-adapter` is a thin TypeScript adapter around the `bd` CLI
(beads issue-graph store), used as Recoder's shared cross-agent memory
substrate. It shells out to the `bd` binary; it does not vendor beads source.

